  <!-- Format.* are RULES, not labels: how this language punctuates, rather than something to
       translate word for word. They live here so adding a language is one file's worth of work —
       the separators used to be `code.StartsWith("zh") ? "、" : ", "` written out in four
       different .cs files, which meant a new language silently got English punctuation in all
       four with nothing to catch it.
       Spaces are written as &#32; on purpose. A trailing space is significant here and an editor
       or an XML tool that trims trailing whitespace would silently change the output. -->
  <Text key="Format.ListSeparator">、</Text>
  <Text key="Format.BulletSeparator">&#32;&#32;·&#32;&#32;</Text>

